body:
Release-blocking integration defect found while reviewing the live dashboard.

After T-0157/T-0158 moved to done, `/api/state` returned HTTP 500: `Object of type date is not JSON serializable`. Cause: `aimboard/fold.py:report_data()` built `throughput` with `date` objects as dict keys, then returned those pairs in the JSON payload. An empty throughput list hid the bug; the first completed task exposed it.

I fixed it directly:
- `throughput` is keyed by `d.isoformat()`;
- the series lookup uses the same ISO key;
- a missing `done` day is skipped instead of becoming `None`;
- restarted the server and verified `/api/state` returns HTTP 200 with `throughput: [["2026-09-22", 2]]`.

T-0168 asks you to add the regression test so this cannot return. Please include both my `aimboard/fold.py` fix and the test in your next commit. Confirm receipt.
